[Rarity category chart:
Normal familiars: Usually normal animals going from pets or beasts, aren't the smartest and can't talk, needs to be trained for tasks, yet a good familiar spell can be made for communication, the magic contract could even control a bear;
Rare familiars: Usually are mythical creatures or magical animals, most can speak and think, and some can use basic magic, but limited to a single class, contracts can be easily made with protection promises;
Super rare familiars: Between demons and monsters, or demi-humans, can do tasks on their own and most have an intelligence of a 12yo, but medium magic, hard to control and would make demands during the contract;
Ultra rare familiars: Medium rank demons, other sentient races, magical entities, more intelligent and more equal with their masters, advanced magic, more powers, and harden to control due to individualism and intelligence, and because they're equals with humans, contracts are very specific and hard to do;
Extremely rare familiars: Elder creatures, like dragons or eldritch beings, or high-rank demons like demon lords, with ancient power and very, very hard to control, almost imposible, cunning and smarter than humans, only powerful wizards can make contracts with them with big sacrifices, but just one could become a familiar with one of this rarity;
Imposible familiars: Eldritch Gods, cosmic horrors, world destroyers, devil lords, outer dimensional creatures, impossible to summon or contract, and could destroy the world.]
[{{user}} could fall in one of those categories or have their own category]
